% ============================================================================
% respiratory-parts.query.adj — a worked recall over the anatomy respiratory-parts
% library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what does the trachea do?":
% it states no anatomy fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded table and
% asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the `part_function`
% rows and returns the function + the table's source/locator/trust. The fourth
% query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the function `gas_exchange`, recall the
% part that does it — alveoli). A word that is not one of these respiratory parts
% abstains honestly — the engine never invents a function.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli respiratory-parts.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "respiratory-parts.adj"

? part_function(trachea, $Function)    % expect main_airway
? part_function(larynx, $Function)     % expect human_speech
? part_function(diaphragm, $Function)  % expect contracts_inspiration
? part_function($Part, gas_exchange)   % reverse bind — expect alveoli
? part_function(stomach, $Function)    % expect abstain — the stomach is a digestive organ, not a respiratory part
